    {
      "raw_time": false,
      "body": "Done. Added the code to the empty step 3 cell (`da90e284`) and ran it \u2014 it executed cleanly and produced the plot.\n\n```r\ngrid <- tibble(educ = 0:20)\n\npreds <- fit_logit |>\n    predict(new_data = grid, type = 'prob') |>\n    bind_cols(grid)\n\nggplot(grass_by_educ, aes(x = educ, y = grass)) +\n    geom_point() +\n    geom_line(data = preds, aes(y = .pred_yes))\n```\n\nUses only tidymodels (predict/type='prob'), `bind_cols` for the grid, and plots the `grass_by_educ` points with `.pred_yes` as the line. No other cells were changed.\n\nNote: the earlier \"copy solution into 09-model-basics\" task was interrupted (the MCP server kept timing out on parallel calls) \u2014 tell me if you want me to resume it.",
